cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this dataset, please cite the dataset itself."
type: dataset
title: "WebMCP Description Benchmarks: Behavioral Eval of In-Browser Tool Surfaces"
authors:
  - family-names: Clouâtre
    given-names: Hugues
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0002-4291-1999"
repository-code: "https://github.com/clouatre-labs/webmcp-description-benchmarks"
license: Apache-2.0
date-released: "2026-10-04"
version: "1.0.0"
abstract: >
  Supplementary dataset for a behavioral evaluation of the WebMCP tool surface
  exposed by clouatre.ca. Three tasks (discover, extract, traverse) x three
  models (claude-haiku-4-5, glm-5.3-flash, gpt-6-luna) x five iterations were
  run across three site configurations (pagination baseline, response caps
  with progressive disclosure, and a tool-response ordering fix), 135 runs
  total, driven through the real document.modelContext registration in
  Playwright Chromium via a streamable-HTTP MCP bridge and the goose agent
  runtime. Includes the harness and summarizer, deterministic rubric results,
  per-run token and tool-call JSONs, a payload token audit at three commits,
  and the enablement spike findings.
keywords:
  - webmcp
  - model-context-protocol
  - mcp
  - llm-evaluation
  - tool-use
  - agentic-ai
  - token-efficiency
  - progressive-disclosure
  - browser-agents
  - reproducibility
